[block
  'ORD-0007-json'
  [ctx
    'the spec of EMS-002'
    '.guidelines/.orders/EMS-002/EMS-002.pgml'
  [/ctx]
  [tgt
    'JSON in a crate of its own under every other, question 4 of the EMS-001 return, answered b'
  [/tgt]
  [ctx
    'JSON sits in glyph-util, which vocabulary.js and stores.js do not import, so glyph-stores keeps a Value of its own with the same six variants, and the envelope converts one into the other'
  [/ctx]
  [cnst
    'the oracle of glyph-json is the platform, JSON.parse and JSON.stringify as the JS engine has them, and its tests are the ones glyph-util held for it'
  [/cnst]
  [cnst
    'a floor crate depends on no crate of the workspace, and every crate may depend on it'
  [/cnst]
  [cnst
    'no projection moves: a refactor of the Rust under the same oracle'
  [/cnst]
  [cmp
    'the crate'
    'glyph-json holds what glyph_util::json held and replaces the Value of glyph-stores, one JSON type for the workspace'
    [ctx[/ctx]
    [cnst[/cnst]
  [/cmp]
